  "Notes": "Conventional first-order metal-spacer-metal (Ag-L-Ag) filter for comparison (calculated)\nSpecification: First-order conventional Fabry-Perot silver filter peaking at 546 nm\nReported: Fig. 12: half-width 6.3 deg phi; Tmin 0.9 % at phi = 60 and 120 deg (text p. 237); spacerless Fig. 11 design has ~10 % higher peak.\nNotes: Ag 0.0641 x 546 = 35.0 nm. The 1.46L spacer accounts for the Ag reflection phase.\nLayers from Fig. 12 caption (h_Ag = 0.0641 lambda); text p. 236; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
